# Compound Growth

> [!orbit] Tutorial Example
> This note was extracted from a source (book) during processing.

---

## One-liner

Small, consistent additions create exponential results over time. The magic isn't in big leaps but in **persistent small steps**.

---

## The Principle

Compound growth appears when:
1. Each addition builds on previous additions
2. Growth is **consistent** rather than sporadic
3. Time is allowed to work its magic

```
Day 1:   1
Day 10:  10
Day 100: Not 100... but 1,000+
```

The non-linear acceleration is counterintuitive but mathematically certain.

---

## Examples

| Domain | Compound Effect |
|--------|-----------------|
| **Knowledge** | Each note makes future notes easier to connect |
| **Skills** | Daily practice builds on previous practice |
| **Relationships** | Small interactions accumulate into deep trust |
| **Writing** | Each published piece builds audience and skill |
| **Forests** | Trees in networks grow faster than isolated trees |

---

## In PKM Context

- **More notes → More connections → More insights**
- **Daily capture → Weekly review → Monthly synthesis**
- **Each link increases future linking opportunities**

This is why consistency matters more than volume. 10 notes/week for a year beats 500 notes in January.

---

## Source

Extracted from [[Tutorial - Source - Thinking in Systems]] - Chapter on reinforcing feedback loops.

Meadows calls these "virtuous cycles" - systems where success breeds more success.

